92186069665 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069972 #edb/ref 1064 "Multiplying rational expressions is just like multiplying fractions. After all, fractions are just rational expressions with constants!\n\nFor example, to multiply the rational expressions\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{x}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{y}{2}\n$$\n\nwe multiply the numerators and the denominators as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{x} \\cdot \\dfrac{y}{2} = \\dfrac{3 \\cdot y}{x \\cdot 2} = \\dfrac{3y}{2x}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069972 #edb/ref 1065 3378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069972 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "9b51617b-96b7-5112-bd91-a351a05ee49a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069972 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
